agent-ops task task-6c58094f-ebc5-43bb-8f64-9153b6ed6005: Pre-implementation criteria advisory review
intent: Implement the agreed bounded criteria-only single-review advisory using existing isolated invocation and process ownership, private snapshot reports and safe logs, all production task creation hooks, no new dependency/config trust/state machine or final proof gate. Five observable criteria are validated with node-test. Final design at /private/tmp/agent-ops-criteria-review-spec-2026-10-23.md and agy consensus at /private/tmp/agent-ops-criteria-review-final-sketch.md.
criteria:
- creation-paths: Every production task creation path, including DEBUG and native run root/child, awaits one advisory criteria review before implementation, without duplicate automatic attempts or live model calls in uninjected fixtures.
- scoped-advisory: A single independent reviewer receives only bounded original goal, assigned intent/covers, criteria and surface data in an empty workspace and returns validated structured recommendations; missing goal and not-yet-existing verification materials remain explicitly unassessed.
- uncapped-cancellable: Criteria review allocates no execution deadline or stall budget, genuine launch/provider/output errors remain advisory, and explicit cancellation stops its process tree and writer startup while preserving the task; other verification and formal review limits remain finite.
- report-provenance: Private reports and safe local summaries expose recommendations, task snapshot and attempt status; revisions preserve a visibly historical report without automatic rereview, explicit rerun creates a new attempt, and report/log failures never roll back task creation.
- final-proof-independent: Criteria advisory never produces or satisfies verification, final dual-review or finish attestations, and the existing final proof, policy and trust contracts remain unchanged.
